# ── Game distribution: binaries & assets ──────────────────────────────────
# The original Theocracy binaries and data are copyrighted and NOT
# redistributable. They must be provided out-of-band, not committed.
#   /linux/    -> theocracy.real, libmvos*.so, server, ... (game dist)
#   /data/cd   -> ~448M ripped CD assets
#   /data/cd-* -> per-release rips: disc images and Redbook audio tracks
#                 (e.g. /data/cd-uk, the UK 2-CD release ripped 2026-08-08).
#                 The glob is deliberate — `/data/cd/` alone does NOT match
#                 `/data/cd-uk/`, and the music rip is as copyrighted as the
#                 disc it came off.
#   /data/game -> ~184M extracted/decrypted game data
# Kept on purpose: /data/*.tsv and /data/mvos_api.json (small derived symbol/
# reloc reference tables the docs depend on; no copyrighted content).
/linux/
/data/cd/
/data/cd-*/
# Ignore the extracted game data, but keep our hand-authored mvos.cfg (normally
# installed by inst.linux; the libmvos cfg loader reads it as data/game/mvos.cfg).
/data/game/*
!/data/game/mvos.cfg
# Philos' post-release `reconf` tool and its tarball — not on the CD, found on a
# holarse.de mirror of the dead dlh.net download. Copyrighted the same as the
# rest, so same rule. Both the root drop and a tidier home under data/ are
# covered; see docs/reference/reconf-tool.md.
/reconf
/*reconf*.tgz
/data/patches/

# Regenerable from git history itself — `python3 tools/dump_commit_log.py`.
/data/commit-log.md

# ── Build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/port/build/
/port/build-linux/
# Per-arch container build trees. The amd64 one was committed by accident in
# 96c3db7 (32 files, including the binary) and untracked on 2026-08-04.
/port/build-linux-*/
/port/build-win/
/port/build-macos-arm64/
# Staged third-party Windows dependencies (SDL2 / Unicorn / ffmpeg headers,
# import libs and DLLs) for the mingw-w64 cross build. Third-party binaries:
# same rule as data/cd/ — fetched out of band, never committed.
/port/deps-win/
build/
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.dylib

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Editor / OS / local ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Profiling / run logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
# tools/plot_health.py output — regenerate it from the log
*-health.svg

# Packaged bundles — rebuild with tools/package-linux.sh
/dist/

# Minimal ffmpeg for the bundles — source tarball, build trees and install
# prefixes. All regenerable with tools/build-ffmpeg-min.sh; third-party source
# and binaries, so the same rule as port/deps-win/ applies: never committed.
/port/ffmpeg-src/
/port/deps-ffmpeg-win/
/port/deps-ffmpeg-linux-*/
/port/deps-ffmpeg-macos-arm64/

CLAUDE.md
